  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "truncate never exceeds max",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "# Objective\nFix `truncate(text, max)` in `src/text.js` so the returned string is never longer than `max` characters, and still ends in `...` when the text had to be cut. Leave `capitalize` and the non-truncating path untouched.\n\n# Steps\n1. In the cut path reserve room for the ellipsis: `text.slice(0, max - 3) + '...'`.\n2. Handle small budgets (max <= 3) so the result is still at most `max` characters and is still an ellipsis marker: return `'.'.repeat(max)`.\n3. Add regression tests in `test/text.test.js` covering exact-fit, one-over, a long string at several max values, and max 0-3. Assert result length <= max and, when cut, that it ends with `...` where max >= 3.\n4. Run `pnpm test`.\n\n# Constraints\n- Only `truncate` changes; `capitalize` and the non-cut path keep their behaviour.\n- No dependencies added.",
      "preview": null,
      "dispatch": null,
